==== Operation Details

.OP-01 -- `CreateInventoryItem`
[cols="1,4", stripes=even]
|===
| Field | Specification

| Performer
| Flutter mobile app, activated by an authenticated household member.

| Input variables
| `userId`, `householdId`, item name or barcode, category, location, quantity, optional low-stock threshold, optional expiration date, shared/personal flag.

| Output variables
| New or updated `ItemType`, `ItemInstance`, `InventoryRecord`, and optional `QuantityChangeTransaction`.

| Domain preconditions
| The household has or is acquiring an item that should be represented in the tracked inventory. Quantity may be exact or approximate. Expiration may be present or absent depending on the item.

| Required preconditions
| User must be authenticated and have permission to add items in the household context. Required item identity fields must be valid. Quantity must be non-negative. If the item is shared, the user must have shared-item update rights.

| Trigger conditions
| User taps *Add Item*, scans a barcode or enters item information manually, and submits the form.

| Required postconditions
| A tracked inventory record exists for the item in exactly one household context. Provided quantity, location, threshold, expiration date, and shared/personal status are preserved. The inventory list refreshes and displays the new item.

| Related goal / requirement
| N1, N2, N3; DG-REQ-01, DG-REQ-02, DG-REQ-03, DG-REQ-04; US-INV-01; IR-01, IR-04, IR-05.

| Related test case
| Proposed: `TC-OP-INV-01`. Existing overlap: `TC-TXN-01` if creation records an initial quantity transaction.

