.OP-02 -- `UpdateItemQuantity`
[cols="1,4", stripes=even]
|===
| Field | Specification

| Performer
| Flutter mobile app / inventory repository, activated by household member.

| Input variables
| `userId`, `itemInstanceId`, current quantity, new quantity or delta, reason code, timestamp.

| Output variables
| Updated quantity/availability, appended `QuantityChangeTransaction`, recalculated low-stock state.

| Domain preconditions
| Consumption, restocking, correction, or adjustment changes item availability. Quantity must never become negative.

| Required preconditions
| User must be authenticated and authorized to update the item. Target item must be active. New quantity or delta must be valid. Concurrent update conflicts must be rejected, merged, or explicitly resolved.

| Trigger conditions
| User edits quantity, taps consume/restock, or a grocery finalization updates quantity.

| Required postconditions
| Item quantity reflects the accepted change. A transaction record is appended with reason and timestamp. Low-stock and out-of-stock state are recomputed. Existing metadata remains stable unless explicitly edited.

| Related goal / requirement
| N2; DG-REQ-02, DG-REQ-03, DG-REQ-04; US-INV-02; IR-02, IR-04.

| Related test case
| Existing: `TC-TXN-01`, `TC-ALT-01`. Proposed: `TC-OP-INV-02`.

