.OP-03 -- `DeleteInventoryItem`
[cols="1,4", stripes=even]
|===
| Field | Specification

| Performer
| Flutter mobile app / inventory repository, activated by authorized household member.

| Input variables
| `userId`, `itemInstanceId`, deletion/correction reason, confirmation response.

| Output variables
| Removed or archived item record, inactive alert conditions, preserved historical records.

| Domain preconditions
| A household item may be consumed, discarded, mistakenly entered, or no longer tracked. Historical spending and transaction records may still matter after deletion.

| Required preconditions
| User must be authenticated and authorized to delete or archive the item. If spending entries or alert records are associated with the item, the system must not silently delete financial history.

| Trigger conditions
| User chooses delete/archive and confirms the action.

| Required postconditions
| Item no longer appears in active inventory. Existing financial history is preserved unless separately corrected. Outdated expiration or low-stock alerts for the deleted item no longer continue firing.

| Related goal / requirement
| DG-REQ-03; US-INV-01; IR-EC-D; expiration/alert deduplication behavior.

| Related test case
| Existing: `TC-EXP-02`. Proposed: `TC-OP-INV-03`.

