.OP-07 -- `GenerateLowStockAlert`
[cols="1,4", stripes=even]
|===
| Field | Specification

| Performer
| Scheduled sweep function / alert service.

| Input variables
| Household inventory state, quantity/availability, low-stock threshold, alert rules, previous alert history.

| Output variables
| New or retained `AlertNotification`, optional grocery-list entry.

| Domain preconditions
| Low-stock judgment is meaningful only when the item has valid quantity/availability data and a configured or default threshold.

| Required preconditions
| Item must be active. Threshold and quantity data must be valid. Alert rules must be active. A duplicate alert for the same item-condition-recipient group must not already exist in the current reminder period.

| Trigger conditions
| Quantity crosses the low-stock threshold, or scheduled sweep observes that the item remains below threshold.

| Required postconditions
| One low-stock alert exists for the item-condition pair within the allowed reminder period. Repeated sweeps do not create spammy duplicates. Alert is visible to authorized household members.

| Related goal / requirement
| DG-REQ-05, DG-REQ-07, DG-REQ-08; US-ALT-01; IR-04.

| Related test case
| Existing: `TC-ALT-01`, `TC-ALT-03`, `TC-AUTO-01`, `TC-AUTO-02`.

