.OP-08 -- `GenerateExpirationAlert`
[cols="1,4", stripes=even]
|===
| Field | Specification

| Performer
| Scheduled sweep function / alert service.

| Input variables
| Item expiration date, current date, near-expiry window, alert rules, previous alert history.

| Output variables
| New or retained expiration-related `AlertNotification`.

| Domain preconditions
| Expiration behavior can only be derived for item instances with valid expiration dates. Items without expiration dates must not produce false expiration confidence.

| Required preconditions
| Item must be active. Expiration date must be present and valid. Alert rules must be active. Deleted or renewed items must not keep emitting outdated alerts. Duplicate alert protection must apply.

| Trigger conditions
| Current date enters the near-expiry window, reaches expiration date, or scheduled sweep observes an expired item.

| Required postconditions
| Item state is classified as active, near-expiry, or expired as appropriate. One non-duplicate alert exists for the item-condition pair within the reminder period. Renewed/deleted items stop producing stale alerts.

| Related goal / requirement
| DG-REQ-06, DG-REQ-07, DG-REQ-08; US-ALT-01; IR-05.

| Related test case
| Existing: `TC-EXP-01`, `TC-EXP-02`, `TC-AUTO-01`, `TC-AUTO-02`.

